From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:53:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [bugs #3153] sdld: accept the line symbols of --debug from
 more than one module

With --debug, cdbWriteCLine() defines a global symbol at each line of C
code. Its name has the base name of the source file, the line, the
level, and the block number, as in C$inline.h$16$1_0$2. Modules that
include a header with a static function define equal names when the
function has the same block number in each of them. The linker reported
"Multiple definition" for each name and the link failed. r12010 removed
the symbols from code that the compiler expands inline, which is the
case of the ticket. The link still failed for static functions, inline
or not.

newsym() now creates a symbol entry for each definition of a name that
begins with C$. The map file and the .cdb file have one address per
module for such a line. The files already had several addresses for one
line when the block numbers of the function differ between the modules,
because the names then differ.

The regression suite links one module per test and does not pass
--debug, so this change does not have a test there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sdas/linksrc/lksym.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sdas/linksrc/lksym.c b/sdas/linksrc/lksym.c
index bb9336f40..0d8448fdb 100644
--- a/sdas/linksrc/lksym.c
+++ b/sdas/linksrc/lksym.c
@@ -167,6 +167,22 @@ newsym(void)
 	} else
 	if (c == 'D') {
 		ev = eval();
+#if SDCDB
+		/*
+		 * SDCC names the symbols for lines of C code
+		 * C$file$line$level$block.  These names are not unique
+		 * when several modules have code from one file, such as
+		 * a static function in a header.  Create a symbol entry
+		 * for each definition.
+		 */
+		if (tsp->s_type & S_DEF && id[0] == 'C' && id[1] == '$') {
+			tsp = (struct sym *) new (sizeof(struct sym));
+			i = hash(id, zflag);
+			tsp->s_sp = symhash[i];
+			symhash[i] = tsp;
+			tsp->s_id = strsto(id);
+		}
+#endif
                 if (tsp->s_type & S_DEF &&
                     !(tsp->s_addr == ev && tsp->s_axp && tsp->s_axp->a_bap && ((tsp->s_axp->a_bap->a_flag & A3_ABS) == A3_ABS))) {
 				fprintf(stderr,
